  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "While Fang Yuan uses Chainsaw Golden Centipede as a spinning razor on his arm, the narration names rank four Chainsaw Killer Centipede as one of the advancement paths of that rank three Gu. Three hundred years later, a new demonic faction talent, Chainsaw Mad Demon, would use it.",
        "chapters": [
          166
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_chainsaw_golden_centipede",
          "char_chainsaw_mad_demon"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Descriptions of saw-teeth, dark gold exoskeleton, and the arm-blade method belong to rank three Chainsaw Golden Centipede.",
        "chapters": [
          166
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "distinct-from-its-predecessor",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan recalls that chainsaw golden centipede had two main advancement routes. One is the rank four chainsaw killer centipede. The other is the flying vajra centipede, which has rank three, four, and five versions. When Gu Masters used these two Gu worms, the former could slaughter strong enemies while the latter could pierce bones and flesh, drilling into the enemies’ body.",
        "chapters": [
          2108
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "two-advancement-routes",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters",
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      }
    ]
